at `x ∈ U`, and the identities `Σ_{pq} C^a_{pq} K^p K^q = 0`, `Σ_a C^a_{pa} = 0` holding on the
whole open `U` (so that they may be differentiated), the registered `ricci` satisfies

  `Σ_{pq} (Ric_Γ − Ric_Γ̄)_{pq} K^p K^q = −2 Σ_{ap} M^a_p B_a^p − Σ_{ap} M^a_p M^p_a`,

`M^a_p = Σ_q C^a_{pq} K^q`, `B_a^p = ∂_a K^p + Σ_c Γ̄^p_{ac} K^c` (`covD`). No curvature library,
no background flatness, no Lorentz signature.

**Main root** (`vii08_ks_ricci_contraction`): for raw `KSData b bi v k U` (non-constant
background allowed) and `x ∈ U`,

  `Ric_g(k,k) = Ric_b(k,k) − v · b(A, A)`,  `A = accel b bi k` (actual VII-07 acceleration),

all with the registered `ricciOf`/`christoffel`/`pd`. In the 2009 convention `v = −2H` this is
`Ric_g(k,k) = Ric_b(k,k) + 2H b(A,A)`. Consequences: actual pregeodesic `k` ⇒
`Ric_g(k,k) = Ric_b(k,k)`; an independent actual background `VacuumCertificate` (Ricci-flat, not
Riemann-flat) ⇒ `Ric_g(k,k) = 0`; and the constructor of the VII-07 `RicciNullPregeodesicField`
(constructed in `KSTailObstruction`) whose `ricci_null` field is an **output** of this
derivation. No converse is claimed (`v = 0`).
-/

